Hi Angela,

Thank you for talking through the trial with us this morning. I have attached=
 the results for circulation, the desk procedure and Connor's separate two-li=
ne check sheet.

Could you check that the seven working days reported for February agrees with=
 your approval record? On the same clock we used for December, 2 March is D1 =
and your approval on 10 March is D7. That compares with nine working days for=
 December, so the trial was two days shorter, but one day beyond the six-day =
target.

The supplier statement arrived after Friday's 15:00 window, but the account w=
as reconciled at 10:25 on Monday, before the 11:00 pack window. The stock ext=
ract received at 09:18 on Monday had no signature; the usable replacement arr=
ived at 11:26 and reconciliation finished at 13:10. That left the pack to cir=
culate on Tuesday. The results explain the two waits separately.

For the next close, please arrange for Accounts Payable to take the supplier =
account line and Stock Finance the inventory cutoff line on the attached shee=
t. The procedure sets out what each desk needs before it can resume. If evide=
nce is missing, could each owner record the hold, who is following it up and =
the next check time, and tell the pack owner what is outstanding? By 11:00 on=
 circulation day, the pack owner should have either completion with its refer=
ence or the hold and next check. You can then review the two lines at the nex=
t close. The next-close actuals are blank until the desks have results to ent=
er.

Best,
Nicholas

